comments[12]:
  - created_at: "2026-07-30T10:27:24.832Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Implementation evidence: graph impact defaults to 10 rows, returns resumable next_cursor pages, rejects unknown cursors and --full plus --limit, while --full explicitly restores the complete impact set."
  - created_at: "2026-07-30T11:24:15.338Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Delivery boundary: impact now defaults to ten rows, resumes through stable cursors, rejects invalid cursor/full-limit combinations, and exposes explicit --full. The canonical issue remains open until the bound is declared in shared contract data and a real-scale structural test asserts every graph subcommand is bounded."
  - created_at: "2026-07-30T11:30:56.402Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "PR evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/829 reviews cohesive SDK context budgets, universal row contracts, bounded graph/health diagnostics, quality ratchets, and exact-head commit e53544cd1."
  - created_at: "2026-07-30T11:54:23.905Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review correction: graph impact cursors are now opaque and fingerprinted by root, direction, kinds, and max depth; mismatched traversal resumes fail with invalid_query_cursor."
  - created_at: "2026-07-30T13:06:11.203Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review-fix evidence for PR #829: TDD reproduced zero-limit graph pagination losing the continuation cursor. Impact pagination now fingerprints a root-anchored cursor when limit=0 so the next request resumes at the first affected row; the new focused zero-limit SDK test passes, and the full sandboxed suite passed 6,578 tests at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage."
  - created_at: "2026-07-30T13:39:03.617Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Exact-head Greptile review evidence: impact cursors intentionally bind traversal semantics rather than page size because resuming with a different limit is lossless. Source docstrings and the public contract documentation now state that callers may raise or lower --limit when resuming; the zero-limit continuation regression remains green and the full 6,579-test exact-coverage suite passes."
  - created_at: "2026-07-30T17:15:05.660Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "Verified shipped 2026-07-30 (evening) at HEAD. graph impact is now bounded by default and the reduction is 144-fold: 2,160 bytes default against 311,343 bytes with the explicit escape hatch, with 988 bytes on the summary form. The default now carries a resumable cursor rather than truncating silently, so the bound is recoverable rather than lossy. Measured on the same item and the same corpus as the original finding, which reported 230,452 bytes and roughly 57.6k tokens as the default.\n\nRecording this as evidence rather than closing the item: the original finding also owns the sibling asymmetry that centrality bounds at ten while analyze reports its sample limit and the ancestor and successor verbs return roughly 205 bytes, and it owns the question of whether the bound is declared in the contract or implied by the command. Whoever closes this should check that the new default appears in the contract output rather than only in the help text, since a bound an agent cannot discover before invoking is still a surprise at first use."
  - created_at: "2026-09-18T15:02:13.900Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Red-first evidence: a real 1000-item sandbox returned 999 ancestors against the expected default 10. Shared SDK graph defaults now bound hierarchy/order traversals and slack critical paths; focused 26-test graph run passes. Impact pagination and explicit full traversal remain available."
  - created_at: "2026-09-18T15:13:27.832Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Live repository graph evidence: all-status CLI snapshot contains 2778 items and graph analyze indexes 13871 deduplicated edges in one connected component, with zero orphans and zero ordering/hierarchy cycles. Execution depth is 12 layers. Audit has two informational findings covering seven terminal-only cardinality and seven terminal-only direction conflicts, with zero active hierarchy conflicts. Existing graph implementation and verification edges retain their concrete meaning; unrelated repository intake is tracked with its canonical owners."
    edited_at: "2026-09-18T15:50:18.214Z"
  - created_at: "2026-09-18T15:19:03.157Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Manual and installed acceptance passed: a disposable CLI workspace created 13 items; descendants returned 10 rows then the final 2 through --after, and --full returned 12. pm contracts declares the same default before invocation. Packed npm/npx/bunx smoke passed with nine installed packages; a separate Bun-installed consumer imported matching GRAPH_QUERY_DEFAULTS from aggregate, graph and contracts SDK entrypoints under Node and Bun. Packed first-run acceptance passed README init/create/list, MCP handshake, concurrent branch merge/history validation and detached telemetry completion with physical queue drain. Initial npm smoke hit host temporary-filesystem EDQUOT; rerunning under an isolated scratch directory on the workspace filesystem passed without product changes."
  - created_at: "2026-09-18T16:12:22.534Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final complete suite passed: 9011 tests across 710 files; exact counts 62071/62071 lines, 64853/64853 statements, 13463/13463 functions and 49478/49478 branches. Rebuilt packed npm/npx/bunx acceptance passes. Static source, contract, SDK import and graph/integrity checks pass. Node 24 transport-floor remains a local limitation: next best 443 ms against unchanged 440 ms limit after a quiet 20-sample run; comparing baseline before attributing a regression."
  - created_at: "2026-09-18T16:15:43.808Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Latency baseline comparison: rebuilt untouched main 14d992008 in an isolated worktree under Node 24.12.0 and the same 20-sample unchanged transport gate. Baseline next best 460 ms exceeds 440 ms; candidate best 443 ms also exceeds 440 ms. This is not evidence of a candidate regression or a local pass. Keep the committed budget unchanged and require the hosted static gate before merge."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-30T09:21:20.690Z","harness:claude-code","Re-measured 2026-07-30 at HEAD, after PR 818 shipped bounded projections. Unchanged in kind and slightly worse in ratio: pm graph impact pm-doxj default = 223,214 B; the same call with --summary = 488 B, a 457x spread. The default still honours no row bound while sibling subcommands do. Bounded projections shipped somewhere else; this default was not among them."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-18T15:15:13.313Z","harness:codex","Bound discovery belongs in reusable SDK contract data and pre-invocation command contracts. Row caps must be applied at the graph projection boundary so analytics continue to see the whole topology. Real-scale tests must enumerate the registered vocabulary: tiny fixtures can make an unlimited traversal appear bounded. CLI continuation intentionally amortizes metadata, so acceptance should verify emitted rows and continuation_contract rather than demand repeated first-page counts."
